## Rules for Interface
* Keeps templates, js, css in separate files.
* Make reusable template components
* Keep styling and html in one file for weasyprint templates.

## Rules for Backend
* Use class based views

## General Rules
* Don't delete anything until told to.
* Templates should only handle display, if any logic or calculation is needed, get it from backend.
* If a template tag is to be loaded for math operations, then that means logic needs to be put in backend and sent via context.
